==Old English==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|gem-pro|ang}} {{recons|þuljanan|lang=gem-pro}}, a weak grade of {{etyl|ine-pro|ang}} {{recons|tel-|lang=ine-pro}}, {{recons|tol-|lang=ine-pro}}, {{recons|tḷ-|lang=ine-pro}}.  Cognate with Old Saxon {{term|þolian|lang=osx}}, Old High German {{term|dolen|dolēn|lang=goh}}, Old Norse {{term|þola|lang=non}} (Swedish {{term|tåla|lang=sv}}), Gothic {{term|𐌸𐌿𐌻𐌰𐌽|tr=þulan|lang=got}}; compare Latin {{term|tuli|lang=la}}, {{term|tolerare||tolerate|lang=la}}, {{term|tollere||lift up, bear|lang=la}}, Ancient Greek {{term|τλῆναι|sc=polytonic|lang=grc}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/θoliɑn/|lang=ang}}

===Verb===
{{ang-verb|type=weak|class=2}}

# to [[suffer]], [[endure]]

